  ],
  "slug": "biomedical-knowledge-modern-49a1",
  "summary": "Recent items pair pretrained molecular encoders with multimodal fusion and constraint-aware generation for property prediction and binder design.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is learned biomolecular representations coupled to a second modality or explicit constraint, spanning prediction and generation. MPMFMol pretrains a molecular graph encoder with fragment-based augmentations and fingerprint multitask learning before multimodal fine-tuning, while HKD-CPI aligns LLM-derived tokens with molecular graphs and applies knowledge distillation. Fusion architectures recur: DMPKformer combines Transformer, GAT, and MLP branches with latent OOD confidence, CM-MTL-DTI uses bidirectional cross-modal attention, and EpiFormer interleaves cross-attention within GNN layers. On the generative side, AlloGen separates backbone generation from a learned SE(3)-invariant state-selectivity scorer, and PepForge generates modified HELM peptides hierarchically. The copolymer MILP inverse-design work does not involve pretrained representations. What appears newer is coupling representations to structural or geometric constraints rather than task-specific training alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-06-03"
}
